From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean Dolbec <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:02:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Add the nub SPMI controller

The main PMU of the T8132 machines sits on the nub SPMI bus at
0x388714000 (macOS: nub-spmi0). Its NVMEM holds the shutdown, boot-stage
and RTC-offset cells that the SMC reboot and RTC drivers need: without
the shutdown flag, the SMC's "off1" restarts the machine instead of
powering it off.

Add the controller, disabled, with its always-on nub_spmi0 power domain
as t8140.dtsi does. Boards add the PMU and enable the bus.

Signed-off-by: Sean Dolbec <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index d211b40d19..be0bec478b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/apple-aic.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/pinctrl/apple.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/spmi/spmi.h>
 
 / {
 	compatible = "apple,t8132", "apple,arm-platform";
@@ -462,6 +463,15 @@
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		nub_spmi: spmi@388714000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8132-spmi", "apple,t8103-spmi";
+			reg = <0x3 0x88714000 0x0 0x100>;
+			#address-cells = <2>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_nub_spmi0>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		smc_mbox: mailbox@38c608000 {
 			compatible = "apple,t8132-asc-mailbox", "apple,asc-mailbox-v4";
 			reg = <0x3 0x8c608000 0x0 0x4000>;
